# Windows batch files must keep CRLF line endings. cmd.exe reads a batch file
# in chunks and resolves `goto` by seeking through those chunks, so with
# LF-only endings a label lookup can land mid-line and fail with "The system
# cannot find the batch label specified" - for some labels and not others,
# depending on where they happen to sit in the file.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
